WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.860
Tokens per second describes approximate generation speed, while prompt-processing speed describes how quickly input context is evaluated.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:17.800
A system can generate quickly yet pause for a long prompt, or process prompts quickly while generating slowly.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:24.279
Batch settings can improve throughput but increase memory use and may affect latency.

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:31.742
Concurrency changes the problem again: several users or jobs compete for compute, cache, and memory.

00:00:31.822 --> 00:00:36.252
Benchmark expected simultaneous demand, not only one ideal request.

00:00:36.332 --> 00:00:43.223
GPU offload moves supported model layers or operations from CPU execution to an accelerator.

00:00:43.303 --> 00:00:50.194
More offload often improves speed until memory pressure, transfer overhead, or backend limits dominate.

00:00:50.274 --> 00:00:52.735
The optimum is configuration-specific.

00:00:52.815 --> 00:00:55.768
Context length should match the application.

00:00:55.848 --> 00:01:01.755
Loading maximum context for short tasks wastes cache and prompt-processing time.

00:01:01.835 --> 00:01:07.249
Retrieval, summarization, code, and chat workloads have different useful context patterns.

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:13.236
Memory pressure can cause allocation failures, swapping, severe slowdown, or service instability.

00:01:13.316 --> 00:01:18.730
Thermal throttling can reduce sustained speed after an impressive short benchmark.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:24.717
Monitor temperatures, clocks, memory, power, latency, errors, and queue depth over time.

00:01:24.797 --> 00:01:32.180
Benchmark practical workloads with representative prompts, output lengths, context, models, quantizations, concurrency, and acceptance criteria.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:35.213
Record quality as well as speed.

00:01:35.293 --> 00:01:44.153
The best setup completes real work reliably; it does not merely win a synthetic tokens-per-second comparison.
